  'tshwane-voters-head-to-polls-4-november-2026-10-26',
  'Tshwane voters head to the polls on 4 November',
  'Community', '2026-10-26', 'SAnews (via AllAfrica)', 'https://allafrica.com/stories/202610260550.html',
  'Tshwane''s 107 wards vote in the local government elections on Wednesday 4 November, a public holiday, with stations open from 07:00 to 21:00.',
  'Voting day for the City of Tshwane arrives this Wednesday, 4 November, when residents choose their new municipal council. President Cyril Ramaphosa has declared the day a public holiday, and the Electoral Commission says voting stations will be open from 07:00 to 21:00. Tshwane keeps its 107 wards from the 2021 election, though the Municipal Demarcation Board has redrawn many of the boundaries: 27 wards are unchanged, 43 have minor adjustments and 37 have been reworked more substantially.

Voters may only cast their ballot at the station linked to the address where they are registered, and postal voting is not an option in these municipal polls. Anyone unsure of their station can use the Electoral Commission''s online Voting Station Finder, SMS their ID number to 32810, or call the commission on 0800 11 8000; SMSing an ID number to 32245 shows a voter''s current ward councillor. Acceptable proof of identity is a smart ID card, an ID book with a green barcode, or a valid temporary identity certificate - a driver''s licence, passport or a copy of any ID document will not be accepted at the station.

Approved special-vote applicants who could not reach a station on election day were able to vote early, on 2 or 3 November, between 08:00 and 17:00, with home visits offered to those who are elderly, pregnant or living with a disability. At the station on 4 November, Tshwane voters in the metro receive two ballots: one to choose a ward councillor and a second proportional-representation ballot, on which 70 parties are standing for seats on the metro council.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://allafrica.com/stories/202610260550.html", "https://www.gauteng.net/whats-on-g/tshwane-wards-2026-local-elections/", "https://www.gauteng.net/whats-on-g/local-elections-4-november-2026/", "https://www.elections.org.za/content/About-Us/IEC-Events/Local-Government-Elections-2026/"]',
  'agent'
);
